# A REQUEST, reconstructed by hand from RFC 8415 section 18.2.2: a DUID-LLT client
# identifier, the server's DUID-UUID, one IA_NA that holds the address the server offered,
# an option request and elapsed time. Documentation MAC 00:00:5e:00:53:02, documentation
# prefix 2001:db8::/32.
#
# msg-type REQUEST, transaction id 0x1d2e3f
03 1d 2e 3f
# option 1, client identifier, 14 octets: DUID-LLT (type 1), hardware type 1,
# time 0x2c3d4e5f (seconds since 2000-01-01), the MAC
00 01 00 0e
00 01 00 01 2c 3d 4e 5f 00 00 5e 00 53 02
# option 2, server identifier, 18 octets: DUID-UUID (type 4, RFC 6355), 16 octets of UUID
00 02 00 12
00 04
00 11 22 33 44 55 46 77 88 99 aa bb cc dd ee ff
# option 3, IA_NA, 40 octets: IAID 0x5e005302, T1 0, T2 0, and one IA Address
00 03 00 28
5e 00 53 02
00 00 00 00
00 00 00 00
# option 5, IA Address, 24 octets: 2001:db8:1::100, preferred 3000 s, valid 4000 s
00 05 00 18
20 01 0d b8 00 01 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 00 01 00
00 00 0b b8
00 00 0f a0
# option 6, option request, 4 octets: 23, 24
00 06 00 04 00 17 00 18
# option 8, elapsed time 100 (one second)
00 08 00 02 00 64
